---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About The Birdie Report | Our Editorial Approach"
  description="Learn who publishes The Birdie Report, how we produce golf coverage, and how we distinguish hands-on experience from research-based analysis."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <header class="text-center mb-16">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">About The Birdie Report</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        Practical golf coverage with a clear line between direct experience, documented research, and opinion.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-12 mb-16" aria-labelledby="publisher-heading">
      <div class="lg:col-span-2">
        <h2 id="publisher-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Published by Kyle Reierson</h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg text-gray-600">
          <p>
            Kyle Reierson founded The Birdie Report to make golf equipment and strategy coverage easier to use. The site publishes buyer guides, product comparisons, instructional articles, course coverage, news, and opinion for golfers who want a direct answer without the usual marketing fog.
          </p>
          <p>
            Not every article is produced the same way. Some coverage can include direct experience; much of the product library is research-based. We do not treat those as interchangeable, and we do not want readers to assume that every product mentioned on the site was purchased or personally tested.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-1">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-6">
          <img
            src="/images/kyle-reierson.jpg"
            alt="Kyle Reierson"
            class="w-full rounded-lg mb-4"
          />
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Kyle Reierson</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Founder and publisher<br />The Birdie Report</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-8 mb-16" aria-labelledby="mission-heading">
      <h2 id="mission-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 text-center">Our Editorial Goal</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        Help golfers understand the meaningful differences between products, make better purchasing decisions, and play smarter—while being candid about what we know, how we know it, and where uncertainty remains.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-16" aria-labelledby="method-heading">
      <h2 id="method-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 text-center">How Our Coverage Is Produced</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Research-based</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
            These articles use sources such as official specifications, product documentation, current pricing, published reporting, and clearly identified golfer-feedback patterns. They are not presented as hands-on tests.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Hands-on</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
            We use this label only when the named author has direct experience with the product or subject. The article should explain the relevant conditions and limits instead of making a vague testing claim.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Hybrid</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
            Some articles combine direct experience with published research. Those pieces should distinguish observed experience from specifications, pricing, and claims supplied by outside sources.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 mb-16" aria-labelledby="standards-heading">
      <h2 id="standards-heading">Editorial standards</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We aim to verify current specifications, availability, and pricing against primary sources where possible.</li>
        <li>We distinguish manufacturer claims from our own analysis.</li>
        <li>We update material errors when we find them and show an updated date when an article materially changes.</li>
        <li>Affiliate relationships do not guarantee favorable coverage. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.</li>
        <li>If an article does not carry a hands-on label, readers should not assume that the product was personally tested.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Corrections and questions</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        Found an error, have a sourcing question, or want to know more about how an article was produced?
      </p>
      <a
        href="/contact/"
        class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 bg-green-700 text-white font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-green-800 transition-colors"
      >
        Contact The Birdie Report
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
